### Summary

**`src/commands_retry.rs** — Added extract_tool_name_from_error()` function:
• Searches error text for known tool names (bash, edit_file, read_file, write_file, search, rename_symbol, list_files, sub_agent, shared_state, `ask_user, todo`) with word-boundary matching
• Longer names checked first to avoid partial matches
• Returns Option<&'static str> — None if no tool recognized

`src/commands_retry.rs` — Updated handle_retry():
• Extracts tool name from the last_error text using extract_tool_name_from_error
• Passes the tool name to the enhanced build_retry_prompt
• Shows more specific feedback: (retrying with edit_file error context + recovery hint) instead of generic `(retrying with error context)`

`src/prompt_retry.rs` — Enhanced build_retry_prompt():
• New third parameter: tool_name: Option<&str>
• When a tool name is provided, the retry prompt now says `"Previous attempt failed — {tool} error: {summary}. {recovery_hint}" where the hint comes from the existing tool_recovery_hint()` function
• Without a tool name, falls back to the original generic message

Tests added (15 new tests):
• extract_tool_name_from_error: tests for edit_file, bash, read_file, write_file, search, rename_symbol, quoted context ('edit_file'), unknown errors, empty input, word-boundary enforcement ("searching" doesn't match "search"), multi-tool preference
• build_retry_prompt with tool name: enriched prompt format, unknown tool fallback, no-error-with-tool-name passthrough
• In prompt_retry.rs: tool name enrichment, bash-specific hint, no-error passthrough

